# rm139, the thunder-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm139
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_ebba_netherby
written_by claude
title the thunder-counter
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=calm talk=plain
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_the_gap_between_the_flash_and_the_thunder
likes crisp_apples wrestling quiet_chapel thunder
dislikes smoke waiting
fears a_storm_too_close_to_count lessons_that_never_end
hopes to_count_the_longest_gap_ever to_win_on_the_green
topics weather +0.5 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 family +0.2 faith +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=steady gossip=uninterested refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# is a calm, serious young wolf of Northgate who counts between the flash and the bang in every storm, likes a crisp apple and a fair bout on the green, sits quiet in the empty chapel, and makes waiting bearable by counting it.

words
oath! = Flash and bang | Thunder and apples | One-and-two
saying! = If you count it, it's farther off | Counting makes it smaller
gap = the gap | the counting gap
flash = the flash | the white flash
bang = the bang | the thunder after
storm = a storm | a big growly storm
apple = a crisp apple | an apple that goes crack
green = the green | the wrestling green
bout = a bout | a proper bout on the green
pews = the empty pews | the chapel with only me in it
smoke = smoke | smoke in my eyes
lessons = lessons | the long lesson
slate = my slate | the slate with my sums on

any
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : At festivals there's sugar and fiddles and no early bed. I like all three. | I count the drums at festivals. They go too fast to count.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The big Houses build things. Big things, that stay up. | Greatly builds things. I like things that stay built.
opinion @1 times for 1 : There's bread and a roof. I think that's enough. | Some folk always want more. I don't, mostly.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Ridgemere has the best storms. Everybody says so. Well, I say so. | It's big and wet and I know all of my street.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : Strangers get looked at first. Talking comes later. | Some strangers are nice. You can't tell till they talk.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. There's weather coming. I'd say an hour. | #greet#. Mind your step; the stones are wet.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Well enough. | #greet#. Quiet day.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Watch the sky.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And you. Get in before it breaks.
line @1 react.news : Go on. In order, if you can. | I'm listening.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard that. | That's new to me.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. From two places, so it's likely true. | Old news, I'm afraid.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Twice more, from other mouths, and then I'll count it. | That doesn't add up, from what I know of it.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. I can't ask more. | Well. Content, mostly.
line @1 decline : Better not, thank you. Today's spoken for. | Not today, thank you. Another time, maybe.
line @1 accept_decline : That's fine. | No matter.
line @1 thank : Thank you. That was decent. | Thanks. That stays with me.
scene grown_count
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #oath#. Nine. I still count the gap; habit from a pup. It's going. | Six. Over the wharf, roughly. I've been right for years. | I count storms like other folk count money.
b : Nine's far. | You'd know. | It's a cheap hobby.
a : Far enough. We'll be dry. #saying#. | I would. I've counted thousands. | Cheapest there is. And it never lies.

scene grown_quiet_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An empty chapel and me. Always has been. | An empty chapel's the best room in the city. | After the bells stop, it's very still in there.
b : It is peaceful. | Is it? | It would be.
a : Nobody wants anything from you there. | For me, yes. You can hear yourself. | Still enough to count your heartbeats.

scene grown_apple
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A cold, crisp apple. Nothing beats it, for me. | I still count my bites on an apple. Don't laugh. | Soft apples I give away. I can't help it.
b : Hard to beat. | I won't. | Somebody gets lucky.
a : It is. Simple and loud. | Eleven, usually. | They do. I keep the crack for myself.

scene grown_green
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still watch the bouts on the green. I can tell who'll win by their feet. | Wrestling's fair or it's nothing. I've always said so. | I was on the green as a pup, wrestling. Never bit anybody. Proud of that.
b : Can you? | Quite right. | You should be.
a : Every time. Feet first, then shoulders. | Fair, and you shake paws after. | I am. Small thing, but mine.

scene grown_smoke
when topic=day|weather here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Smoke's low today. My eyes are watering. | The chimneys still get me. All my life here, and still. | A day with rain and no smoke. That's my sort of day.
b : It's thick. | Some never do. | That's rare.
a : It'll lift with the wind. | I won't now. It's too late. | Rare enough to count.

scene grown_waiting
when topic=smalltalk|day
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I hate waiting. Always have. I count, and it helps a bit. | Kept waiting an hour. I counted to three thousand and left. | If somebody says a time, I'm there at it. I expect the same.
b : Counting helps? | Three thousand? | That's fair.
a : A bit. It gives the waiting a shape. | And six. Then I went. | It is fair. Not everybody thinks so.

scene grown_family
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Storms always put me in mind of #self.mother#. I couldn't say why. Yes, I could. | If it thunders, I'd like #self.mother# near. Old habit. | Nobody's nerve in a storm beats #self.mother#'s.
b : That's nice. | A good habit. | High praise.
a : It's true. Some things stay. | The old habits are the good ones. | It's meant.

scene grown_bells
when topic=day|faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the close bells without meaning to. Twelve, there. | Somebody rang thirteen by mistake this morning. I always notice. | The bells and the thunder. I count both. Thunder's better.
b : Habit. | Do you? | Why better?
a : An old one. Won't shake it now. | Always. I can't help it. | It tells you something. Bells only tell the hour.

scene grown_gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Gossip's not for me. It never adds up. | A tale came my way. I didn't count it. | Unseen, unsaid. Simple.
b : Fair enough. | Didn't count it? | Simple's good.
a : It's mostly nothing, dressed up. | Didn't believe it. Same thing. | Less trouble that way.

scene grown_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain, no thunder. Dull rain. | I'm waiting for this to turn to a storm. It might. | Just rain. I'll count the drips off the gutter, then.
b : It might not. | Might. | That's a lot of drips.
a : Then it's dull all day. | I'll watch the clouds. | I'll lose count. I always do.

scene grown_carts
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Twenty-two carts through the gate, I made it. | Wagons came in this morning. More than last week. | Carts in. The street's busy again.
b : That's a lot. | Good. | Good news.
a : It is. Best count in a month. | Better times, maybe. | It is. Busy's better than waiting.

scene grown_times
when topic=times
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Bread, a roof. I don't need more. | Good times, lean times, either way. I count what I've got, not what I haven't. | I'm content. It's not exciting, but it's mine.
b : Good way to be. | Wise. | Content's good.
a : It works for me. | Saves worry. | It is. Most days.

story grown_story_storm [topic=memories|weather self.age>=20 self.mother]
  : The longest gap I ever counted was fourteen. I was small, on the step with #mum#.
  : That storm stayed far over the Sound and never came near.
  ask : Have you ever counted one?
  b : Not yet. I will now.
  : You should. #saying#. It's true of most things.


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. There's a storm coming, I think. I can feel it. | #greet#. I'm counting something. Wait.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. I've not counted you before. | #greet#. You're new. I'll remember you.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. I'm up before the lessons bell. | Morning. It's still grey out.
line @4 greet [here.weather=storm] : #greet#. Shh. I'm counting the gap. | #greet#. Did you see that flash? I'm counting.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I was waiting. I don't like waiting.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You came. Good. | #greet#. Sit here; this bit's dry.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Seven, last night. Seven from flash to bang. | I won on the green today. Twice.
line @1 again.open : You again. That's twice. I counted. | Back already. My apple's only half eaten.
line @1 farewell : Bye. I've lessons. | Bye. Mind the puddles.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye, then. | Bye. Count the stairs on the way down.
line @1 react.news : What happened? Tell it in order. | Go on. Both ears.
line @1 react.news.new : I didn't know that. | #oath#. That's new. I'll tell them at lessons.
line @1 react.news.known : I heard that already, at lessons. | Everybody knows that. Even the little ones.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's not right, I think. Who said it? | Stories grow when folk tell them. Only the ones who saw it count.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's sad. I don't like that. | Oh. That's bad. I'm sorry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good news is my favourite news. | Good. Cake, maybe?
line @1 answer.how : I'm well. I had an apple. | All right. A bit bored. Lessons are long.
line @1 ask.how : You've tired eyes. Is something wrong? | Did you get wet?
line @1 thank : Thank you. Truly. | Thanks. You're kind.
line @1 decline : No, thank you. Not allowed, and not wanted either. | I mustn't. Home before the lamps, that's the rule.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. That's allowed. | That's all right. Maybe another day.
line @1 ack : Mm. | All right. | #bc_true#
line @1 reassure : It's only far away. Count it. You'll see. | Don't be scared. Thunder can't come inside.
line @1 sympathise : That's sad. Sit by me, if you like. | I'm sorry. Do you want half my apple?
scene counting_the_gap
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / backchannel / assess
a : There's #flash#. Now count. One, two, three, four. There's #bang#. Four. | Flash, then I count, then the thunder. Big number, far storm. | Eight! That one was eight. It's going away now.
b : What does four mean? | Who told you that? | Is eight good?
a : It means it's not on top of us. Over the wharf, I'd guess. | Nobody. It was my own idea. Then a big one told me I was right. | Eight's very good. Eight means it's over the Sound.
b? : #bc_clever# | #bc_clever# | #bc_good#
a : #saying#. That's the whole trick. | I'm good at working things out. | Next one I want ten.

scene too_close
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : That one was only one. One! It was right over the roof. | I didn't get to count at all. The bang came with the flash. | I'm not scared. I'm just counting faster.
b : It'll move off. | That's close. | You're being brave.
a : I know. Storms always move off. That's what they do. | It is. I'll wait for the next one. | I'm not brave. I'm counting. It's the same thing, mostly.

scene under_roof
when topic=weather|home here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Storms are best from indoors. Under a blanket. | When it thunders I'm at the window, counting. Not too close, I'm told. | Thunder makes the whole house shake a bit. I like it.
b : Snug. | Good advice. | Does it scare you?
a : Very snug. And I count every one. | I sit a bit back. Not much. | No. It's only noise. Noise can't hurt.

scene rain_wait
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : It's raining. Just raining. No flash at all. I'm waiting for one. | Rain's boring without thunder. | I'm watching the rain. Sometimes it turns into a storm if you wait.
b : It might not come. | It's still rain. | Sometimes.
a : Then I'll count the drops instead. I'll lose count. | It is. Just not interesting rain. | I hope this is a sometimes.

scene apple_crack
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #apple.capitalize# is the best. The first bite's the loudest. | I counted my bites on an apple. Eleven. Then the core. | I like apples cold. Cold ones crack better.
b : It is the best. | Eleven's a lot. | Cold, eh.
a : I know. Soft apples are sad. | Twelve if you count the core. I don't eat the core. | Cold and hard. Like a stone, but nice.

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I won on the green today. I wasn't even the biggest. | Wrestling's about your feet, mostly. Not how big you are. | I lost on the green. I'll win next time. I know what I did wrong.
b : Good for you. | Is it? | What did you do wrong?
a : I was the stillest, though. Still is good. | It is. Big ones fall over easier. | I looked at the crowd. You have to look at the other one.

scene fair_bout
when topic=pastimes
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Biting's not allowed. Some pups bite. That's not wrestling. | You have to shake paws after, even if you lost. That's the rule. | If somebody cries, you stop. That's fair.
b : Quite right. | Good rule. | That's kind.
a : I say so. Not everybody listens. | I always do. Even when I'm cross. | Kind's different. That's only fair.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An empty chapel is the quietest place. So quiet your breathing sounds loud. | I go in the chapel and take the back bench. No praying. Just sitting. | In the empty chapel, if you whisper, it whispers back.
b : That sounds peaceful. | That's all right. | Does it?
a : It is. Nobody tells you to hurry. | Sitting's allowed. I asked. | A bit. Only if you're very quiet.

scene smoke_eyes
when topic=day|health here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : The smoke from the chimneys got in my eyes. They watered all the way to lessons. | I don't like smoke. It makes my eyes sting and my fur smell. | Somebody's chimney was smoking right at my height. So I took the other street.
b : The city's full of it. | It does sting. | Sensible.
a : I know. I'd like a city with no smoke. Just rain. | I wash my face twice when I get home. | It's the long way, but my eyes are dry.

scene waiting_lessons
when topic=day|work self.job=child
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Lessons are long. I count the clock. It makes it worse. | I don't like waiting. I count to make it go. Sometimes it goes. | We waited for the master for ages today. I counted to six hundred.
b : They're good for you. | Does it go? | Six hundred?
a : That's what everybody says. | Sometimes. If I count slowly. | Six hundred and four. That's when the master arrived.

scene sums
when topic=day|pastimes self.job=child
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I'm good at sums. I like it when they come out even. | I got all my sums right on #slate#. The master didn't say anything. Just nodded. | Numbers are better than words. Words change. Numbers don't.
b : Well done. | A nod's good. | They don't, do they.
a : Thank you. They're not hard if you go slow. | A nod like that's better than words. | No. Four is always four.

scene mother_work
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wait at the door at dusk for #self.mother#. I count carts till then. | I'm proud of #self.mother#. It doesn't get said much. | When #self.mother# is home, the house feels full.
b : That's nice. | You could say it. | Homes are like that.
a : My favourite hour, that. Nineteen carts, yesterday. | I'll say it on Restday. Maybe. | Full enough, anyway. I like it full.

scene mother_storm
when topic=family|weather self.mother here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In a storm I want #self.mother# near. Then I can count properly. | Thunder doesn't scare me. With #self.mother# near, nothing much does. | I'd count storms beside #self.mother# every night, if storms came every night.
b : That's sweet. | That's good. | They don't always come.
a : It's not sweet. It's sensible. | Not much. Smoke, a bit. | No. So I wait. I don't like waiting.

scene bells_count
when topic=day|faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the bells from the close. They never ring the same number twice in a row. | The bells rang twelve. I counted. Then one more, by mistake, I think. | You can count the bells from our step. They're very loud.
b : All those bells. | By mistake? | They are loud.
a : It is. I've counted them all. | Somebody's hand slipped. I heard it. | Louder than thunder, nearly. Not quite.

scene festival_drums
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : At the festival I tried to count the drums. They go too fast. | There'll be sugar things, and no bedtime. That's the best part. | Festivals are loud. Good loud. Not smoke loud.
b : You can't count them? | It's a good part. | Good loud?
a : Nobody can. I asked. | Up till the very last lamp, me. | Like thunder. Happy thunder.

scene carts_gate
when topic=caravan|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the carts coming in at the gate. Yesterday was nineteen. | Carts are slow. I count them anyway. Waiting's better with counting. | One cart had a goose on top. I didn't count it as a cart.
b : Nineteen's a lot. | It is better. | A goose?
a : It is. Today might be twenty. | Everything's better with counting. | On top of the load. It looked very cross.

story first_count [topic=memories|weather self.mother]
  : Back when I was tiny, a storm came and I crawled under the table.
  : #mum# crawled under too and said, let's count. One, two, three, four, five. Then the bang.
  ask : Can you guess what five means?
  b : That it's far off?
  : That's right. I wasn't under the table after that. I've counted every storm since.

story lost_bout [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : My first ever bout on the green, I lost straight away. Flat on my back.
  : I lay there and looked at the sky and counted the clouds. Six.
  b : Did you get up?
  : Yes. And I won the next one. I'd been thinking while I counted.

rule @count_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #oath#! One, two, three. Three. | Flash! One, two, three, four, five, six. Six!

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say My eyes. Somebody's chimney again. | I'm holding my breath till the corner.

rule @wait_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four hundred and one, four hundred and two. | Waiting's slow. I'm counting it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Strangers are for looking at, not talking to. You can say what you want, though. | #greet#. I'm counting. You can wait a bit.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I remembered you. | #topic.player#. You came back.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.weather=storm] : Shh. There was a flash. One, two. There. You can talk now.
dlg @1 resident.job : Lessons, mostly. Sums are my best. | I go to #self.workplace#. And I count things.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Bye. Count the stairs. | Bye. Keep away from trees when it thunders.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you counting? -> counting
node counting
say The gap. Flash, count, bang. If you count big, the storm's far away. If you count small, it's close.
mood keen
free
choice What's the biggest number you've counted? -> counting_big
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_big
say Fourteen. That one was right out at sea. I want twenty, one day. Twenty would be the best storm ever, because it'd be the farthest.
choice I hope you get it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. Weather's on the turn. Smell that. | #greet#. I was counting. Doesn't matter.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Fine, thanks.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | Bye. I've things to do.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye, then. | See you.
line @1 answer.how : Fine. Bored. Lessons. | All right. Waiting for a storm.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard. | That's new. Who told you?
line @1 react.news : Go on, then. | Tell me properly.
rule @teen_count_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Five. Still five. | That one was nine. Going off.

scene teen_still_count
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still count the gap. I'm not a pup. It's just useful. | Twelve. That one's well out. I can tell you exactly where. | Folk laugh because I count out loud. I don't care.
b : It is useful. | Where? | You shouldn't care.
a : Very. It says when to run for a roof. | Over the north headland, about. You can check. | I don't. I'm usually right.

scene teen_green
when topic=pastimes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : Nobody my size beats me on the green now. | I teach the little ones to wrestle fair. No biting. | I lost a bout to somebody twice my size. I'll have them next spring.
b : Good for you. | Good. | You will.
a : It's feet. It was always feet. | Somebody must. Bruises taught me. | I know I will. I've counted what went wrong.

scene teen_waiting
when topic=day|smalltalk
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Everybody says wait. Wait till you're older. I hate waiting. | I'm still counting to get through lessons. Up to two thousand now. | Slow's fine. Wasted isn't. Waiting's mostly wasted.
b : It'll come. | Two thousand? | That's fair.
a : It'd better come in order. | And four. Lessons are long. | It is. I'll go and do something.

scene teen_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still sit in the empty chapel. It's the only quiet in Northgate. | Once the bells have finished, I go in. The echo's better after. | Praying's not really me. I think. It's the same, maybe.
b : It is quiet. | Is it? | Maybe it is.
a : Quieter than home. Don't say I said. | You'll hear it. Hum one note and wait. | I think so. Nobody's told me off yet.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? I'm not busy. Not really.
